      [],
      "This capstone course in neural engineering design is the culmination of the NE curriculum. It features market research, the development of a working prototype device or process, along with entrepreneurship in the neural engineering field. The course takes students through the identification of a problem, prototyping solutions, testing, and solution analysis for real world problems focusing on end-user value and benefit. Students will use principles of design, engineering analysis, and customer discovery. This course emphasizes effective teamwork and technical communication, intellectual property, quality, human factors, FDA regulation, professionalism, and ethics. The overall goal of the course is to prepare the students for careers in Neural engineering.",
      []
